<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Is Naz Reid Paid $23.28m?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Reid is paid <strong>$23.28m</strong> because he turned into a center who shoots from distance, and Minnesota paid to keep him before Charlotte took the contract on.</p>
<ul>
<li>He won Sixth Man of the Year in 2024, which is the award that repriced him.</li>
<li>A seven-footer who takes and makes threes changes how a defense has to set up, and clubs pay a premium for it.</li>
<li>He went undrafted, so his first four seasons were cheap and Minnesota had his rights when the market caught up.</li>
<li>He can play either big position, which keeps him on the floor next to another center.</li>
<li>The final season is a player option, so he controls whether he returns to the market at 30.</li>
</ul>
<p>He earns about 26 times what he was paid in his first NBA season.</p>

</div><div class="bde-shortcode-506-159 bde-shortcode"><div class="nba-fin" data-nba-fin="why">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/_ported/08ba6176394a.css">
<script src="/_ported/8334868131c3.js" is:inline></script>
</div>
</div>
</div><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-146 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-shortcode-506-192 bde-shortcode"><div class="nba-fin" data-nba-fin="why_photo">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/_ported/08ba6176394a.css">
<script src="/_ported/8334868131c3.js" is:inline></script>
</div>
</div>
</div>
