<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/naz-reid/#faq","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/naz-reid/"},"mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Is Naz Reid’s Salary in 2026-27?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Reid earns $23.28m in 2026-27, second on the Charlotte payroll behind Coby White. It follows the $21.55m he was paid in the first year of the deal. His career earnings come to $77.89m across eight seasons, all but this one spent at Minnesota. The salary is 14.40% of Charlotte’s $161.69m payroll."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What’s Next for Naz Reid Beyond 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The contract runs to 2029-30, with that last season a player option he can decline. Charlotte owes him $78.17m across the three seasons after this one if he plays them all. He turned 27 in August."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Does Naz Reid Earn Over Time?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A $23.28m season is hard to picture, so here's what it comes to over smaller stretches of time."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Naz Reid’s Contract With the Hornets?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Reid signed a five-year contract worth $125m on July 14, 2025, with every dollar guaranteed and a player option on the final season. Minnesota signed it using his Bird rights, and Charlotte took the contract on when he arrived. He declined a player option worth about $15m on June 27, 2025 to get to that deal, which turned one season into five and raised his pay by roughly $7.5m a year. The option on 2029-30 puts the last decision in his hands."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Is Naz Reid’s Net Worth?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Published estimates put Reid’s net worth at around $3m. That number reads as a stale one against $77.89m in career earnings, most of which has arrived since 2023. He went undrafted out of Louisiana State in 2019 and started on a two-way contract. Six of his first seven seasons paid less than what he now earns in a month."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why Is Naz Reid Paid $23.28m?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Reid is paid $23.28m because he turned into a center who shoots from distance, and Minnesota paid to keep him before Charlotte took the contract on. He earns about 26 times what he was paid in his first NBA season."}}]}</script>
